subproblem.statement:
Let n >= 1, l >= 0, p > n, U any set, V a contract rectifiable n-varifold in U with weight mu, H : R^(n+l) -> R^(n+l) any function, z in R^(n+l), and r, rho real with 0 < r <= rho and B_r(z) contained in B_rho(0) (closed balls). Write K(xi, sigma) := V.scaledLpNorm H p xi sigma = (ofReal(sigma^(p-n)) * lower integral over B_sigma(xi) of |H|^p d mu)^(1/p), a value in [0, infinity]. Then:
(K1) K(z, r) <= K(0, rho);
(K2) for every delta >= 0 with K(0, rho) <= ofReal(delta) and mu(B_r(z)) < infinity, the Bochner integral over B_r(z) of |H| d mu is at most delta * rho^(n/p - 1) * mu(B_r(z))^(1 - 1/p), with mu(B_r(z)) taken as a real number.

Let n, l >= 0, U, U' any subsets of R^(n+l), V a contract rectifiable n-varifold in U, V' one in U', and zeta in R^(n+l). Assume:
- V'.weight is the push-forward of V.weight under tau(x) = x - zeta;
- V'.mult x = V.mult(zeta + x) for all x;
- V'.tangentProj x = V.tangentProj(zeta + x) for all x.
Then:
(R1) V'.weight(B_s(0)) = V.weight(B_s(zeta)) for every real s (closed balls);
(R2) V'.tiltExcess 0 s T = V.tiltExcess zeta s T for every s and every subspace T;
(R3) V'.scaledLpNorm (x -> H(zeta + x)) p 0 s = V.scaledLpNorm H p zeta s for every H, p and s;
(R4) if 1 <= V.mult holds V.weight-a.e., then 1 <= V'.mult holds V'.weight-a.e.

Let n, l >= 0, U any subset of R^(n+l), and V a contract rectifiable n-varifold in U with weight mu, such that y -> V.tangentProj y is mu-a.e. strongly measurable. Let zeta in R^(n+l), T a linear subspace with orthogonal projection P_T, and E(zeta, s, T) := V.tiltExcess zeta s T = (s^n)^(-1) times the Bochner integral over the closed ball B_s(zeta) of hsNormSq(V.tangentProj y - P_T) d mu. Then:
(T1) for every s > 0 with mu(B_s(zeta)) < infinity, the lower integral over B_s(zeta) of ofReal(hsNormSq(V.tangentProj y - P_T)) d mu equals ofReal(s^n E(zeta, s, T));
(T2) for 0 < sigma <= s with mu(B_s(zeta)) < infinity, sigma^n E(zeta, sigma, T) <= s^n E(zeta, s, T);
(T3) E(zeta, s, T) >= 0 for every s > 0.

Let n, l >= 0, U any set, and V a contract rectifiable n-varifold in U with weight mu such that y -> p_y := V.tangentProj y is mu-a.e. strongly measurable. Let q be a linear isometry of R^(n+l), u : R^n -> R^l continuous on a set Omega in R^n, F(x) := q(graphPoint(x, u x)), Du(x) := fderiv u x, and for linear A let P_A be the orthogonal projection onto q(span{graphPoint(v, A v)}). Assume:
(E1) for every Borel A contained in Omega and every Borel g : R^(n+l) -> [0, infinity], the lower integral over A of g(F(x)) dx is at most the lower integral over F(A) of g d mu;
(E2) p_{F(x)} = P_{Du(x)} for Lebesgue-a.e. x in Omega.
Let S be a linear subspace, z in R^n, r real and s > 0 such that:
- the closed ball B_r(z) is contained in Omega;
- hsNorm(Du(x)) <= 1/4 and |F(x) - F(z)| <= s for all x in B_r(z);
- P_{Du(z)} = S.starProjection;
- mu(B_s(F(z))) < infinity.
Then the lower integral over B_r(z) of ofReal(hsNormSq(Du(x) - Du(z))) dx is at most ofReal(s^n V.tiltExcess (F(z)) s S).

Let n, l >= 0, U any set, V a contract rectifiable n-varifold in U with weight mu and p_y := V.tangentProj y, q a linear isometry of R^(n+l), u : R^n -> R^l, and R, rho real. Let Omega := B^o_R(0) (open ball of R^n), F(x) := q(graphPoint(x, u x)), Du(x) := fderiv u x, and, for linear A, P_A := orthogonal projection onto q(span{graphPoint(v, A v)}). Assume:
- u is C^1 on Omega, u(0) = 0, and ||Du(x)|| <= 1/7 for x in Omega;
- F(Omega) is contained in B^o_rho(0);
- y -> p_y is mu-a.e. strongly measurable;
- (E1_Omega) for every Borel g : R^(n+l) -> [0, infinity], the lower integral over Omega of g(F(x)) dx is at most the lower integral over F(Omega) of g d mu;
- (E2) p_{F(x)} = P_{Du(x)} for Lebesgue-a.e. x in Omega.
Then the lower integral over Omega of ofReal(|u(x) - Du(x)x|^2/|x|^(n+2)) dx is at most ofReal(2^(n+4)) times the lower integral over B^o_rho(0) of ofReal(|y - p_y y|^2/|y|^(n+2)) d mu(y). Real division by 0 gives 0.
